---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StoreBadge from '../components/StoreBadge.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Love Desire"
  description="Why we built a couples app for two, not a social platform for many."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-20 pb-16">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-muted font-bold mb-3 text-center">About</p>
    <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-tight text-burgundy text-center">
      For two,<br />
      <em class="font-normal">not for many</em>.
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-16 flex flex-col gap-8 text-burgundy/85 leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <p>
        Most apps that touch relationships end up looking like everything else — feeds, matches, streaks, points, notifications for the sake of notifications. That works for platforms with millions of strangers. It doesn't work for you and one other person.
      </p>

      <p>
        Love Desire is built for the couple who\'s already found each other. There\'s no discovery layer, no friends list, no way for anyone outside your pair to see anything you do here. You share a 6-digit invite code with your person once, and then it\'s just the two of you inside.
      </p>

      <p>
        The features are structured around what actually keeps people close: <span class="italic">rhythms</span> (mood check-ins, Sunday Check-in, Moments), <span class="italic">play</span> (Truth or Dare, Would You Rather, Fantasy Wishes, Activity Cards), and <span class="italic">quiet insight</span> (The Lovers intimacy quiz, Sensate Focus, Relationship Pulse). Some of it is silly. Some of it is deep. Together, they give you a place to keep noticing each other.
      </p>

      <p>
        We treat privacy the way we\'d want it treated. Your data is only visible to you and your partner. We don\'t sell it, share it, or use it to train anything. Explicit content sits behind an 18+ attestation and a paid subscription — one that covers both of you, because subscription belongs to the couple, not the individual.
      </p>

      <p>
        Love Desire is a small independent project. If it helps two people choose each other one more time, it\'s doing what it was built to do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-border">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-24 text-center flex flex-col items-center gap-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl text-burgundy max-w-xl leading-tight">
        Try it with the person you\'re already choosing.
      </h2>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <StoreBadge />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
